y and i use  google calendar a lot so i'm always  swiping over here to make sure i know  where i'm at for the day  and that's it that's the whole two  screen setup for the way i keep my  android phone nothing too crazy of  course all the way over to the left of  those home screens there's google now  and all my cards i use google voice  search all the time from the home screen  but the cards are pretty useful too  looks like clippers beat the spurs the  other night so that's pretty dope and  yeah i feel like pretty much anyone can  emulate this setup if they wanted to  real quick i'll hop over into my app  drawer for some other apps that i don't  have on my home screen so not a billion  apps or anything as you can tell but uh  i do let's see i have apple music i  don't really use it that much but i have  it because you know soundcloud and  spotify are obviously really good i got  some pretty standard stuff in between i  do have the yahoo fantasy sports app uh  currently dominating in nba fantasy  league if you're wondering no big deal  also i do have a little bit of a  phillips hue setup going on in my office  as you probably already know i've been  considering checking out lifx which is a  very similar thing after some  recommendations of it but i also saw a  pretty baller looking beta hue app  coming up soon so i want to check that  out before i switch up my hardware  there's also the nba game time app i  have league pass i watch clipper games  go clippers  uh  periscope do people still periscope i  stole periscope sometimes i feel like  whenever i log on there there's not a  whole lot happening but every once in a  while i do a live show for whatever fun  reason we come up with worth following  there over on periscope if you haven't  already i also have this app called  screener so this is pretty cool i'll  show you actually you can basically make  really pretty looking home screen  showcase images just by inserting it  onto an image of the actual device so  you 